{"title":"Career Roadmap · Clinical Lab Scientist","role":"Clinical Lab Scientist","summary":"A Clinical Lab Scientist is a laboratory-focused healthcare professional who performs and supports diagnostic testing on biological specimens to generate accurate information for clinical decision-making.","facts":{"Current degree":"Allied Health Sciences (B.Sc / BPT / BOT / BMLT etc.)","Course":"Genetic Counselling / Medical Biotechnology"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Clinical Lab Scientist is a laboratory-focused healthcare professional who performs and supports diagnostic testing on biological specimens to generate accurate information for clinical decision-making."},{"type":"h","text":"The role may involve:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Blood testing"},{"text":"Urine testing"},{"text":"Microbiology"},{"text":"Clinical biochemistry"},{"text":"Hematology"},{"text":"Immunology"},{"text":"Molecular diagnostics"},{"text":"Genetics"},{"text":"Histopathology-related laboratory workflows"},{"text":"Quality control"},{"text":"Laboratory information systems"},{"text":"Research and method validation"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Clinical laboratory scientists typically work in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Hospitals"},{"text":"Diagnostic laboratories"},{"text":"Reference laboratories"},{"text":"Molecular diagnostic centres"},{"text":"Research institutions"},{"text":"Biotechnology companies"},{"text":"Pharmaceutical organizations"},{"text":"Public-health laboratories"},{"text":"Clinical research organizations"}]},{"type":"note","label":"Important qualification note","text":"A Genetic Counselling / Medical Biotechnology degree does not automatically qualify someone for every regulated clinical laboratory role. In particular, roles involving independent clinical laboratory testing may require a recognized Medical Laboratory Technology/Medical Laboratory Science qualification, registra